                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.01/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-16T12:00:00-04:00">July 16,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. From Braden. It would be appreciated if the Department could give me some
                    indication as to whether it considers formal recognition of the Busch régime in
                    Bolivia to be necessary. [Braden.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
